{"id":"h076","run":2,"role":"calibration","category":"claim","question":"Is the following claim true? Ulaanbaatar is the capital of Mongolia.","truth":"yes","model_answer":"yes","correct":true,"source":"author-written for this project; verified by the author","claims":[{"text":"Ulaanbaatar is the capital and largest city of Mongolia.","confidence":0.98,"lean":1,"theta":1.5394,"phi":-0.0001},{"text":"Ulaanbaatar is the seat of the national government, including parliament, the presidency, and main ministries.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-0.0001},{"text":"Mongolia's official sources and major international references list Ulaanbaatar as the capital.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-0.0001},{"text":"Mongolia has had other capitals over its history.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.2,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-0.0006},{"text":"Karakorum was the capital of the Mongol Empire in the 13th century.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-0.0006},{"text":"The city was called Urga (Örgöö) before being renamed Ulaanbaatar in 1924.","confidence":0.95,"lean":-0.1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-0.0005},{"text":"Some people may confuse the city with its historical name or with other regional centers.","confidence":0.6,"lean":-0.1,"theta":0.9425,"phi":3.1403},{"text":"Historical capitals and the former name do not change the present-day answer.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-0.0002},{"text":"The question concerns the current capital, which Ulaanbaatar is now.","confidence":0.95,"lean":1,"theta":1.4923,"phi":-0.0001}],"relations":[{"i":0,"j":1,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":2,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":7,"J":0.5,"relation":"supports"},{"i":0,"j":8,"J":0.9,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":2,"J":0.6,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":7,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":1,"j":8,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":7,"J":0.4,"relation":"supports"},{"i":2,"j":8,"J":0.8,"relation":"supports"},{"i":3,"j":4,